{
 "version": "0.4.0",
 "effective": "2026-07",
 "note": "v1 vocabulary built from a labelled statement sample + known Disney POS names. category:null = venue-only rule: identifies the merchant but defers category to L3/L4 (folio-style descriptors are inherently ambiguous). forecast_modeled (2026-07-20): transportation rules the forecast engine already prices with its own term (parking addon, cruise fare). forecastTrip carries only UNFLAGGED transportation actuals, so flagging prevents a double count. Airlines (2026-07-20): the engine cannot predict airfare (it does not know where a household flies from), so airfare is disclosed as excluded and carried from actuals the moment the user records one. Prefixes are deliberately narrow - AMERICAN AIR not AMERICAN (Amex), UNITED AIR not UNITED (United Way), FRONTIER AIR not FRONTIER (Frontier Communications). OTAs (Expedia/Priceline) are intentionally absent: they bundle hotel+air and would guess wrong. Cruise fare = LODGING (the design director 2026-07-20, overrules the earlier fares->transportation mapping): the stateroom is where you sleep and on land+sea the ship replaces hotel nights, same logic as the frozen DVC-dues=lodging. Filing it under Travel made a cruise trip read as if the family never stayed anywhere.",
